target/
.cargo-target/
.cargo-registry/
.pnpm-store/
node_modules/
apps/frontend/dist/
apps/frontend/node_modules/
# 011-api-docs-site: the docs stage builds everything it needs from source inside the image, so a
# developer's local build output and generated inputs must not ride along in the build context —
# these are gitignored for the same reason. `docs/api/` (the vendored upstream OpenAPI document and
# the hand-written sidecar) IS an input and is copied explicitly by the Dockerfile.
docs/dist/
docs/.astro/
docs/node_modules/
docs/public/openapi.json
docs/dist-swagger/
docs/dist-sdk/
docs/public/favicon.svg
.git/
.github/
specs/
*.log
.env*
# Runtime data (compose.yaml's own bind-mount source) — never part of the build context. Besides
# being pointlessly huge (the manga library itself), a rootless-podman uid-mapped subdirectory
# under here (data/database/appendonlydir, owned by Redis's in-container uid) isn't even readable
# by the host user building the image, which fails the build outright without this exclusion.
data/

# Locally fetched PDFium (mise run fetch-pdfium); images fetch their own in the `pdfium` stage.
.pdfium/
dist/native
.native-assets
